course: dictionary
lesson: 3866
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «fraise» has a French meaning and a rare English meaning. In French lessons, «une fraise» is a strawberry, and it is said like «frez» to an English ear. You will mostly meet it on French menus and in French sentences about food.
explain: «Diabolo fraise is strawberry» means the fizzy lemonade with strawberry syrup. Look at the words around the word: diabolo is a drink, and the menu is full of flavours. These clues help you work out what fraise means.
explain: In English, fraise is rare. It appears in history books. A fraise can be a stiff frilled collar like a ruff, or a fence of sharp stakes around a fort. Think about the topic of the text. A castle or an old portrait makes the history meaning more likely.
fact: «Une fraise» means a strawberry in French.
fact: «Fraise» is said like «frez» to an English ear.
fact: «Fraises des bois» means wild strawberries.
fact: In English, a fraise is a stiff frilled collar like a ruff.
fact: A fraise can also be a fence of sharp stakes around a fort, or a tool for widening a hole.
exercise: «Une fraise is a strawberry.» What does «une fraise» mean? | A fizzy lemonade | A blueberry | A raspberry | *A strawberry
exercise: A diabolo is fizzy lemonade with a syrup. Which flavour is «diabolo fraise»? | Vanilla | Chocolate | *Strawberry | Mint
exercise: At an ice cream shop you hear «Quel parfum ?». What does it mean? | Which colour? | Which price? | *Which flavour? | Which perfume is the nicest?
test: «Une glace» is an ice cream. What is «une glace à la fraise»? | A raspberry ice cream | A vanilla ice cream | A lemon ice cream | *A strawberry ice cream
test: In an English history book, a fraise is a stiff frilled collar. What is it like? | A scarf | A cape | *A ruff | A hat
exam: «Une framboise» is a raspberry. Which fruit is «une fraise»? | A cherry | A blueberry | A raspberry | *A strawberry
